[statement]
A later name whose one candidate is reached only through the package an
override would choose does not steer an earlier name to it: `so:h` goes to
`p`, which provides it at version 5; `l` 7, the other candidate, needs
`dav`, whose one candidate needs `l=7`, which would hold `so:h` beside
`p`. apk installs `p` alone. With `dav` required by `app` too, it installs
`dav` and `l` instead. The shape of `reduced/octave-keeps-an-installed-libheif`.
Observed; the rule is not yet known in full.

[repository]
P:app
V:1
D:so:h

P:p
V:1
p:so:h=5

P:l
V:7
p:so:h=1
D:dav

P:dav
V:7
D:l=7

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install p 1
install app 1
